ithub.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.46-47/GitLama-0.1.0-beta.46-47-windows-x86_64.msi"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":31803495,"file":"gitlama-0.1.0-beta.46-47.x86_64.rpm","format":"rpm","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"8ae225a5839b0e61e151addd898ffea3b3987f1099e8be239831a1e34a9de491","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.46-47/gitlama-0.1.0-beta.46-47.x86_64.rpm"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":31807624,"file":"gitlama_0.1.0-beta.46-47_amd64.deb","format":"deb","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"0c438e65913585ef2b6e13d0ec3b8d999056119fb05578d37c0639100379cc34","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.46-47/gitlama_0.1.0-beta.46-47_amd64.deb"}],"build":47,"channel":"beta","notes":["Scrolling to the end of a diff now shows its last line in full: the horizontal scrollbar no longer covers it."],"tag":"v0.1.0-beta.46-47","version":"0.1.0-beta.46"},{"assets":[{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":30349816,"file":"GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-linux-x86_64.AppImage","format":"AppImage","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"4d3e235035baaee6b59876e9546ad48218249314b894d8fcdca89642fd249ab4","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-linux-x86_64.AppImage"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":31760069,"file":"GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-linux-x86_64.tar.gz","format":"tar.gz","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"148ef77002407ec4766276c184ea8e51667c90f5e366d202307456ccc679ca24","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-linux-x86_64.tar.gz"},{"architecture":"arm64","bytes":33844841,"file":"GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-macos-arm64.dmg","format":"dmg","minimum_system":"macOS 13.0 and Git 2.39","platform":"macos","sha256":"69a6c1188022465b0d7f86675ecbf4758e8e546b9eb5d89bfa2983ddb5fecdea","update_signature":"XQLhF2aQzqoQ5GEFPSSkoewEHVrmvl2ZTdGE4AjGytjPCZGksvTmlD3G2kX4qtp65KJ8xlGou+i8AhnAVW+DDA==","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-macos-arm64.dmg"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":27521024,"file":"GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-windows-x86_64.msi","format":"msi","minimum_system":"Windows 10 version 1809 and Git 2.39","platform":"windows","sha256":"8d2befb447643a079732467b0127253af34faf82e9e94f98a1033d8f061d9343","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/GitLama-0.1.0-beta.45-46-windows-x86_64.msi"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":31802899,"file":"gitlama-0.1.0-beta.45-46.x86_64.rpm","format":"rpm","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"9ba6c4311d8f1cc16ea1e17cf5dddf4c717b6b7bddc730352fe653f32989bb82","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/gitlama-0.1.0-beta.45-46.x86_64.rpm"},{"architecture":"x86_64","bytes":31800310,"file":"gitlama_0.1.0-beta.45-46_amd64.deb","format":"deb","minimum_system":"glibc 2.35 and Git 2.39","platform":"linux","sha256":"bde433ff2815084b2d289975de8a318cd8a710576daa93a992120f9beaa9927e","url":"https://github.com/devmil/gitlama/releases/download/v0.1.0-beta.45-46/gitlama_0.1.0-beta.45-46_amd64.deb"}],"build":46,"channel":"beta","notes":["Long lines in the conflict resolver are no longer cut off: they wrap by default, or scroll sideways when you turn wrapping off. The Take current and Take incoming buttons now sit above the side they take, and pointing at a side highlights it and shows what a click will do.","Stage and unstage whole files even when their combined diff is too large to preview. Large files also no longer exceed an in-memory limit when preparing Discard or Clean. Failed actions now show a message that stays until you dismiss it, and appear in the Logbook with a support report you can copy. Reports contain failure codes and build information, without repository contents, paths or credentials. Hosts receive an updated remote helper on their next connection.","Diffs now highlight code syntax in History, Changes and inspector windows, for repositories on this computer and on other computers. The text appears at once as before and the colours follow a moment later, without slowing down scrolling, selecting or staging. Hosts receive an updated remote helper on their next connection.","Dialogs that only show information or let you manage something, such as Hosts, keyboard shortcuts and About, now close with the ✕ in their top corner, like Settings.","Dismiss all in the Logbook now clears every warning, including those from other computers, and dismissing a single entry slides it away smoothly. Showing a new file's changes no longer adds a warning to the Logbook. Hosts receive an updated remote helper on their next connection.","Image changes now preview SVG graphics with blur, shadow, pattern and mask effects. When an image cannot be previewed, GitLama says why.","Repository tools, Snapshots and the custom commands settings are tidier: clear section headings, even spacing, results and facts laid out like the rest of the app, and a guided \"Find a breaking commit\" search that asks plain questions. File sizes now read like \"47 KB\" instead of long byte counts, and many messages avoid Git jargon such as \"index\" or \"HEAD\".","Choosing single lines to stage, unstage, discard or turn into a patch now looks like the diff itself: line numbers, coloured added and removed lines and a checkbox beside each change. Tick a section header to take the whole section, and see how many lines you have picked, with Select all and Select none.","Many smaller dialogs are clearer and calmer: About GitLama is redesigned, confirmations to run a diff renderer or another program show the program and its limits as simple facts with the exact command tucked away, the hosting setup guide is a numbered list of steps, the merge-or-rebase choice explains both options, and undo, restore and discard confirmations use plainer words. The Create patch / Apply patch switch no longer stretches across the dialog, and adding a line comment to a review now says \"Add to review\".","Pushing, pulling, deleting tags and branches, creating repositories, worktrees and patches, and editing hosts use cleaner forms: labels sit above fields, options explain in plain words what they do (for example \"Overwrite the remote branch\" instead of force push with lease), and lists of remotes or files are tidy and bounded. Server keys, LFS pointers and patch previews show their details as clear facts.","A dropped commit in the interactive rebase editor is now struck through only as far as its text.","Long names in lists, such as branch names in the restack review, are no longer cut off while there is still room; the shorter text beside them gives way first.","Rebasing, restacking, merging, cherry-picking, reverting and restoring a snapshot ask clearer questions. Each dialog says in one sentence what will happen, lists branches, steps or files tidily, keeps Git details tucked away, and only warns when something actually needs your attention.","Creating a stash is clearer. Choose between all changes and only selected files; the file list looks like the Changes list and has Select all. The options now say in plain words what they do.","The Logbook filter no longer cuts off its labels, also at larger text sizes, and the timeline line now continues through the selected entry.","In the command palette, the search field no longer runs into the esc hint.","The \"Create patch from this diff\" button in the diff toolbar now sits at the right edge, and narrow diff panes keep the toolbar controls clear of it."],"tag":"v0.1.0-beta.45-46","version":"0.1.0-beta.45"}],"schema_version":1,"trust":{"checksum":"sha256","manifest_signature":"Ed25519 detached signature over exact JSON bytes","signature_encoding":"base64"}}
